.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-SEAL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-seal
.Nd seal a folder of files into a signed capsule
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis seal
.Fl k Ar key
.Op Fl p Ar key.pub
.Op Fl m Ar json-file
.Op Fl -tsa Ar url
.Ar dir
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis seal
turns the folder
.Ar dir
into a capsule
.Pq Xr noqtis-capsule 5 .
It lists every regular file under
.Ar dir ,
computes each file's size, SHA-256 and SHA3-256, writes the manifest
.Pa noqtis.json
(canonical JSON, RFC 8785), signs its exact bytes with the secret key in
.Ar key
under the context string
.Ql noqtis-capsule-1 ,
and writes the seal
.Pa noqtis.sig .
An existing
.Pa noqtis.json
and
.Pa noqtis.sig
at the top of
.Ar dir
are left out of the listing and replaced.
On success it prints
.Dl sealed Ar dir No with Ar alg
.Pp
The folder must hold only regular files and folders with portable names.
Nothing is written, and the exit status is 2, when it holds a symbolic
link, a Windows reparse point, a device, pipe or socket, a name that is
empty, holds a control character,
.Ql / ,
.Ql \e
or
.Ql \&: ,
is not valid UTF-8, or two paths that differ only in ASCII case; or when it
exceeds a limit: more than 2,000,000 files, a path over 4096 bytes, folders
more than 64 levels deep, a manifest over 512 MiB, or a file over
2^53\-1 bytes.
.Pp
The creation time in the manifest is
.Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
when it is set (a decimal number of seconds), otherwise the clock.
.Pp
The secret key and the public key must be one pair: the new seal is
verified before it is written, and a key pair that does not match is
refused.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl k Ar key , Fl -key Ns = Ns Ar key
A secret signature key file (ML-DSA or SLH-DSA).
.It Fl p Ar key.pub , Fl -pub Ns = Ns Ar key.pub
The matching public key, stored in the seal.
Default:
.Ar key Ns Pa .pub .
.It Fl m Ar json-file , Fl -meta Ns = Ns Ar json-file
A JSON object (at most 1 MiB) stored, in canonical form, as the
manifest's
.Ql meta
field and covered by the signature.
noqtis does not interpret it.
.It Fl -tsa Ar url
Reserved for an RFC 3161 timestamp from a time-stamping authority.
This build does not request timestamps: the option fails with
.Dq algorithm or option not supported
(exit 2) and nothing is written.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
Seconds since 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z to record as the creation time,
for reproducible capsules.
A value that is not a plain decimal number is refused.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ar dir Ns Pa /noqtis.json
the manifest
.It Ar dir Ns Pa /noqtis.sig
the seal
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the capsule was written; 2 on a usage error, keys that are not a
signature key pair, an unsealable folder, a limit, or a file that cannot
be read or written.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis keygen -a ML-DSA-65 -o me
ML-DSA-65 key pair: me (secret), me.pub (public)
$ echo '{"project":"demo"}' > meta.json
$ noqtis seal -k me -m meta.json results
sealed results with ML-DSA-65
$ ls results
data  noqtis.json  noqtis.sig  report.txt
.Ed
.Pp
A reproducible capsule:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=1767225600 noqtis seal -k me results
sealed results with ML-DSA-65
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-keygen 1 ,
.Xr nqseal 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
